# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows checkout, so without a rule here every
# LF-ending file git touches is flagged as modified with an empty diff. That is
# not cosmetic: three workflow files sat in `git status` looking like in-flight
# work for long enough to nearly be excluded from a cleanup pass.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto` would ask git to guess
# text-vs-binary across 1000+ tracked files including ~53 MB of images and eight
# .woff2 fonts, and renormalise the whole repo in one commit. These four rules
# cover the files that actually flap.
#
# eol=lf is load-bearing for shell scripts: scripts/android-build.sh runs under
# WSL, where CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
